  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KAIPTC, Kofi Annan International Peacekeeping Training Centre II - KAIPTC, II (2)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">KAIPTC,Kofi Annan International Peacekeeping      Training Centre II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KAIPTC is an official regional center for peacekeeping missions to ECOWAS. It is West Africa&apos;s Institute for Conflict Prevention and Peace and Security Studies at the operational level. The center holds courses for military, civilian and police personnel involved in peacekeeping missions across the world, and conducts research on the causes and subsequent management of conflicts</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">KAIPTC &#xe4;r ett officiellt regionalt center f&#xf6;r fredsbevarande insatser &#xe5;t ECOWAS. Det &#xe4;r V&#xe4;stafrikas institut f&#xf6;r konfliktf&#xf6;rebyggande och freds- och s&#xe4;kerhetsstudier p&#xe5; operativ niv&#xe5;. Centret h&#xe5;ller kurser f&#xf6;r milit&#xe4;r, civil och polisi&#xe4;r personal som deltar i fredsfr&#xe4;mjande insatser &#xf6;ver hela v&#xe4;rlden, och forskar om orsaker och efterf&#xf6;ljande hantering av konflikter</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KAIPTC:s mission for the strategy period of 2014-2018 is:&quot;KAIPTC provides globally-recognised capacity for international actors on African peace and security through training, education and research to foster peace and stability in Africa&quot;The four objectives for the same period are:1. To enhance the capacity of ECOWAS, AU, UN and other relevant actors in multi-dimensional peacekeeping and peace-building (integrated peace support operations) through training2. To deepen understanding of and discourses on critical peace and security issues in Africa through research and policy engagements3. To contribute to knowledge creation that informs best practice in conflict prevention, management and resolution in Africa4. To ensure an efficient, effective and responsive governance and management system in the Centre</narrative>
  </description>
